  "chapter": {
    "number": 44,
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "hebrew_subtitle",
        "content": [
          "(45) For the end, for",
          {
            "noteId": 81
          },
          "alternate strains by the sons of Core; for instruction, a Song concerning the beloved."
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 1,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "My heart",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "noteId": 82
          },
          {
            "text": "has uttered a good matter: I declare my works to the king: my tongue is the pen of a quick writer.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 2,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "You are more beautiful than the sons of men: grace has been shed forth on your lips: therefore God has blessed you for ever.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 3,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Gird your sword upon your thigh, O Mighty One, in your comeliness, and in your beauty;",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 4,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "and bend your bow, and prosper, and reign, because of truth and meekness and righteousness; and your right hand shall guide you wonderfully.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 5,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Your weapons are sharpened, Mighty One, (the nations shall fall under you) they are in the heart of the king's enemies.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 6,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Your throne, O God, is for ever and ever: the sceptre of your kingdom is a sceptre of righteousness.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 7,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "You have loved righteousness, and hated iniquity: therefore God, your God, has anointed you with the oil of gladness beyond your fellows.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 8,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Myrrh, and stacte, and cassia are exhaled from your garments, and out of the ivory palaces,",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 9,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "with which kings' daughters have gladdened you for your honor: the queen stood by on your right hand, clothed in vesture wrought with gold, and arrayed in various colors.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 10,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Hear, O daughter, and see, and incline your ear; forget also your people, and your father's house.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 11,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Because the king has desired your beauty; for he is your Lord.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 12,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "And the daughter of Tyre shall adore him with gifts; the rich of the people of the land shall supplicate your",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "noteId": 83
          },
          {
            "text": "favor.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 13,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "All her glory is that of the daughter of the king",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "noteId": 84
          },
          {
            "text": "of Esebon, robed as she is in golden fringed garments,",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 14,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "in embroidered clothing: virgins shall be brought to the king after her: her fellows shall be brought to you.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 15,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "They shall be brought with gladness and exultation: they shall be led into the king's temple.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 16,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Instead of your fathers children are born to you: you shall make them princes over all the earth.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 17,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "They shall make mention of your name from generation to generation: therefore shall the nations give thanks to you",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "noteId": 85
          },
          {
            "text": "for ever, even for ever and ever.",
            "poem": 1
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "footnotes": [
